not_code_range_buf: for a range starting at U+0000, from - 1 wraps to 0xFFFFFFFF under an encoding whose multibyte
ranges start at 0 (UTF-16/32), so a nested negated class holding U+0000 gains every code point. UTF-8 Oniguruma,
and so vscode-oniguruma, never shows it (GregsEx issue #16; aikawayataro/Onigwrap#16).

